            <ArticleTitle>Ophthalmoplegia with headache. Be aware of diabetes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>161-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cranial neuropathy affecting the eyes is a possible symptom of type II diabetes. In this article, Dr Dickerman describes a case in which diabetes was diagnosed in a 63-year-old woman who presented with unilateral headache and eye pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
